#: ../../catalog_model.md:65 89c5480bdc6d4c58b7f6add6132d33a1
msgid "How it becomes a Shopify product"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:67 82e5f53c931448719f848f7b0a929087
msgid "`create_product_shopify` and `update_product` build it the same way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:69 f70227a2720d43cdb2be2fa1aa562ae8
msgid ""
"**Shopify product** = the Model (title, descriptions, photos, vendor = "
"Marque, product type = Type). Its Shopify id is stored in Annonces "
"Shopify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:71 a8bd5d97071a46218f1e9a0a53e32737
msgid ""
"**Shopify options**: `État esthétique` always. A second option is added "
"only if a Variation has a `Variant_value`, and its label is hard-coded "
"from the Type: \"Plage de volume [µL]\" for micropipettes, \"Dimensions "
"[cm]\" for paillasses, \"Variante\" for anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:75 d3e81f7219654cfb93899cf5496aa426
msgid ""
"**Shopify variant** = one per *(Variant_value, Etat esthétique)* pair "
"found among the sellable units. Sellable means `Statut commercial = A "
"vendre` and a condition other than Abimé/Très abimé."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:78 5d178ccbc47a46a4b285069b1c991c62
msgid "**Quantity** = the number of those units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:79 f73542510a46461c89875e387977c6f0
msgid "**Price** = the lowest `Prix de vente HT` among them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:80 4137bee838d44273b4230445171b8e54
msgid ""
"**Spec table** (`main_table` metafield) = weight, dimensions, and the "
"Specifications of the **first** Variation only, minus its variant spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:83 44c39a8518824971a36e594cc5d3e7ed
msgid ""
"So **stock and price come from units, structure comes from Variations, "
"and content comes from the Model.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:94 f5a16bff8d73491bb03c19f295bfff0b
msgid "Creating a product we've never had"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:111 fd858e4b1af54db9b90d1fe218b5a5ca
msgid ""
"The `create-rewake-model` skill automates the Model + Variation + "
"Specifications part. In the receiving workflow, the app does it through "
"`/internal/catalog`: operations push the group (a variant Variation gets "
"its axis spec through `Spec_variant`), and the commercial team reviews "
"the Model (`Vérification pour site`) before it is sold; see [Catalog "
"intake](catalog_intake.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:118 91838b8c000545ab89ddd3e34009347a
msgid "Rules that the scripts rely on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:120 43cc7c19235d45fcb2187dae05950c19
msgid ""
"**Every unit needs exactly one Variation** (`Référence variant`). A unit "
"without one is invisible to Shopify and to the reconciliation (52 such "
"units today, plus 1 linked to two Variations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:123 433e0062c1af46f695f1c360690441f5
msgid "**Every Variation needs exactly one Model** (5 have none today)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:124 ae3ef3fdd4584442bf054cf5777ae679
msgid ""
"**A Model is either all `Non` (one Variation) or all `Oui`.** Never mix "
"them: a `Non` Variation next to `Oui` ones would end up as a Shopify "
"variant whose option value is `0`. No Model mixes them today."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:127 b81627797467483892f3339c1e2c6418
msgid ""
"**`is_variant = Oui` needs a `Variant_name`.** 5 Variations break this "
"today, and 3 have `is_variant` empty. The intake push refuses a variant "
"without its axis (`missing_variant_axis`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:130 454f687b173e45e6a08e1992ba2b3265
msgid ""
"**Only one dimension can vary.** `Variant_name` holds a single spec, so a"
" pipette range can be a variant axis, but \"range × number of channels\" "
"can't. Make those separate Models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:133 29e9c4fafbf54bb0b4be8317a583505f
msgid ""
"**Specs that differ between versions, other than the variant axis, are "
"lost on Shopify.** Only the first Variation's specs go into the spec "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:136 1815407163d940be99019cc74d70d68f
msgid "The weak spots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:138 0ef8850c58f64d2aad0084f6e5b8336f
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**The default Variation duplicates the Model.** For 94% of Models it's a "
"copy of the Model that exists only so units have something to link to. "
"It's created automatically, so it costs no work, but it's still a second "
"record per product, and it's where the Model's specs end up (see the next"
" point)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:142 69bed8fde1b84516abb2f276061669b7
msgid ""
"**Specs are copied for every Variation.** A 10-version pipette has 10 "
"copies of \"Nombre de canaux : 1\", which have to be kept consistent by "
"hand. Only the first copy is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:145 5b3abb75cff341779137c22293b88b54
msgid ""
"**`is_variant` is typed by hand** (the API only sets it on the records it"
" creates or converts) but can be worked out from the data (`Variant_name`"
" filled or not), so it drifts (8 inconsistent records)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:148 2a19d4a1443a4f13ad333d65d8a55c91
msgid ""
"**The second option's label is hard-coded** by Type name in the code "
"(`_variant_option_name` in `api/scripts/_shopify_links.py`), so a new "
"Type with versions just gets \"Variante\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:151 99d6d5528cdc4de888b6e180e4648f86
msgid ""
"**Prices live in two places.** Each unit has its own `Prix de vente HT` "
"(what Shopify uses), and the Variation also has `Prix bon état €HT`, "
"`Prix abimé €HT` and `Prix de la variation`, which nothing in the API "
"reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:155 cecee06b8d904ef995a3b292dd64885b
msgid "Suggested improvements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:157 4193ca73b592485ba884860e9eac3e34
msgid ""
"They are ordered from cheapest to most structural. Each one can be done "
"on its own, without changing what Shopify shows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:160 f8d0aa246e7d4da59fc74d10273eaa6f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Make `is_variant` a formula:** `IF({Variant_name}, \"Oui\", \"Non\")`. "
"The code only compares it to `\"Oui\"`, so nothing breaks, and the 8 "
"inconsistent records disappear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:163 d0ea457259a547f7aa453b7dd9980c9c
msgid ""
"**Add data-quality views,** and have the reconciliation flag the same "
"cases: units without a Variation, Variations without a Model, Models that"
" mix `Oui` and `Non`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:166 55684c15422b43a7badc1913abd1e270
msgid ""
"**Move the variant label to the Type:** add an \"Axe de variante\" field "
"on Type d'équipement (e.g. \"Plage de volume [µL]\") and read it instead "
"of the hard-coded names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:169 880d560e4a32419d8e95eae2c07686af
msgid ""
"**Put common specs on the Model:** link Specification to Model for what "
"all versions share, and keep on each Variation only the spec that defines"
" it (`Variant_name`). This removes the copies (most of the 8,106 records)"
" and the \"first Variation only\" rule, and the spec table reads Model "
"specs + the variant value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:174 9d3539e938444dc8877e7dc95d809567
msgid ""
"**Keep the default Variation.** It's already created automatically, so "
"the duplication costs no work; what it still costs is the specs stored on"
" it, which suggestion 4 moves to the Model. Removing the level altogether"
" (units linking straight to a Model) would mean two different ways for a "
"unit to find its Model and two code paths in every script, so a Variation"
" that always exists is the simpler rule: **Model → ≥1 Variation → "
"units**, always."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:180 f905415ab8704e35bee58a308a729589
msgid ""
"**Choose one source of truth for price:** either the unit's `Prix de "
"vente HT` (today's behaviour), with the Variation prices removed or "
"turned into suggestions, or a price per (Variation, condition) that is "
"copied onto new units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_model.md:185 ae8b4b64f4ee4839b24253ffafc2a6c5
msgid ""
"The condition stays on the unit. It describes one physical item, and the "
"current mapping to Shopify (condition = an option, units = quantity) is "
"right."
msgstr ""

